    "body": "An alternative integration of the type-hole-inference work (PR #1872) with current `dev`, branched from commit `0b9d841ca9` instead of the #1872 tip. Per feedback from the original author, this **excludes the \"tpats now use type provenances\" experiment** (the commits from `65433eeb6f` onward), which had integrated TPat-as-provenance too deeply. Compare with #2290, which was based on the tip and carried that experiment through the elastatics merge.\n\n## What this includes / excludes\n\n- **Included:** Typ-level type-hole inference \u2014 annotated `type_provenance_t`, constraint-returning `Typ.meet`, the `Inference.solve` monolith, the `TypeHole` projector, and the inference pipeline wired end-to-end through dev's elastatics statics.\n- **Excluded:** the TPat-solving experiment. `tpat_term` stays the conventional `Invalid | EmptyHole | MultiHole | Var` (matching dev), so there is **no** TPat-as-provenance, no `TypeSubstitution` provenance, and none of the deep TPat integration. The inference module stays the single `inference/inference.re` (not the experiment's `inference/` split).\n\nBecause the TPat grammar matches dev, the elastatics merge is dramatically cleaner than #2290: `Equality.re` and `Abbreviate.re` don't even conflict, and there are zero TPat-pattern rewrites.\n\n## Commit sequence (for review)\n\n1. `35a4dbf` \u2014 merge `dev` into the `0b9d841ca9` base (conflict resolution; build intentionally not green yet)\n2. `71e8d0c` \u2014 post-merge build fixes: annotated-provenance threading, `Prov`/`equivalence` in TermBase, inference monolith adapted to dev's new sorts (`DrvQuoteTy`/`Projector`/`Sig`), `MatchedTyp` provenance patterns, inference wired into `mk_with_inference`/`CachedStatics`\n3. `817db6c` \u2014 `dune fmt` + fix three `==`-against-fresh-provenance comparisons (bulk-rewrite artifact) to proper shape matches\n4. `6c741cf` \u2014 bump CI test timeout 20m \u2192 40m\n\n## Resolution strategy\n\n- **dev wholesale** for the elastatics-rewritten `Statics` / `Info` / `StaticsBase` / `CustomStatics` and the restructured test suite; deletions accepted for `Self` / `Elaborator` / `helpful-assistant` / `Test_Info` / `Test_Evaluator_Probe`.\n- **Manual merge** of the term layer: kept the base's annotated `type_provenance_t`, constraint-returning `meet`, and `matched_*_of_prov` helpers; took dev's `Mod`/`Sig`/`MPat` sorts, `DrvQuoteTy`, and conventional `TPat`.\n- **Glue** (`CachedStatics` / `CachedSyntax` / `ProjectorInfo` / `ProjectorView` / `CodeEditable` / CLI) threads the inference map (`Inference.SolutionMap`) and `sample_focus` through dev's structures.\n\n## Inference wiring\n\n`Info.exp`/`Info.pat` carry a `constraints` field. `Statics.add` records the subsumption equivalence `Con(ana, elab_syn_ty)` plus the structural constraints `Typ.meet` emits. `mk_with_inference` aggregates all Info constraints (deduped by representative id) and runs `Inference.solve`, returning the solution map that `CachedStatics` exposes and the TypeHole projector consumes. (Per-handler `MatchedTyp` constraint emission \u2014 the \"quality improvements\" from #2290 \u2014 is intentionally NOT carried here; `MatchedTyp` stays dev's 2-tuple form, and constraints flow via the core `meet`/subsumption path. Worth a follow-up if inference precision needs it.)\n\n**Build green across src + tests; all 2688 tests pass.**\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
